module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.green_reported_over_a_population_the_instrument_does_not_own

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data green_reported_over_a_population_the_instrument_does_not_own: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "green_reported_over_a_population_the_instrument_does_not_own" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an instrument reports GREEN over a population it does not own, so a fact can be filed in an authority, absent from the projection readers are pointed at, and nothing refuses** (INVALID STATE: two actuators split one generated-artifact population, and the one lanes habitually run denominates only its own half. ",

    "`claim_executor --required-regen` reports `first_generation_equal=true planned=155 executed=155 adjudicated=155` while `docs/design-failure-modes.md` is STALE, because the ledger projections are produced by a different actuator entirely -- `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/gunbc/instruments/generated_artifact_gate.dag --function main_wet`. ",

    "HARM: a lane files a row in `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode`, runs the regen, sees 155/155/155, and stops -- having shipped a row that exists in the authority and nowhere a reader can see it, since DESIGN.md points readers at the projection and not at the .dag. ",

    "The green is not merely uninformative about the projection; it is READ as covering it, because the instrument's name and its round numbers make no distinction between the population it adjudicated and the population it was asked about. ",

    "SPECIMEN, and it is the row filed beside this one: `absence_classifier_default_bucket` was authored into the authority, `--required-regen` returned first_generation_equal=true, and the projection still did not contain it. ",

    "The gap was found by GREPPING THE PROJECTION for the row just filed, which is not a step any gate performs. ",

    "THE TWO NEIGHBOURS THIS IS NOT, cited so the family is readable and this row is not consolidated into either. ",

    "[[incidental_denominator_as_wall]] is THE SAME DENOMINATOR SHAPE WITH THE OPPOSITE SIGN: there, `is_compared_generated_basename` -- whose job is to denominate the DRIFT COMPARISON -- accidentally CREATED safety by never handing an installer a dangerous input, so nothing is wrong today and the harm is that the protection is uncredited and dissolves silently when the upstream question changes. ",

    "Here the same accident runs the other way: a denominator written for one question accidentally DESTROYS COVERAGE while continuing to report green, and something IS wrong today. ",

    "Uncredited protection versus credited assurance that is not there. ",

    "[[authority_merges_unprotected_while_its_projection_is_guarded]] is a MERGE-TIME protection asymmetry over the same file pair -- projection driver-bound, hand-authored authority matching no merge attribute -- repaired by binding the driver to the authority path. ",

    "This row is REGEN-TIME and is reachable with no merge in sight. ",

    "(Two notes worth keeping. ",

    "That merge row landed in the very merge that conflicted the branch filing this one, and it had already measured the 16,792-character line 144 that made the conflict hazardous -- the hazard was filed by another lane before this one hit it. ",

    "And it has since been observed firing in production on a SIBLING lane's head: `git merge-tree --write-tree` returned rc=1 with BOTH projections refusing while `gh pr view` reported mergeable=MERGEABLE on that same commit, observed simultaneously -- a cleaner specimen of that row than the one it was filed with, and a second instrument disagreeing with a green.) A SECOND SPECIMEN, RECORDED BECAUSE THE AUTHOR OF THIS ROW COMMITTED THE SAME SHAPE WITHIN THE HOUR OF FILING IT, IN THE OPPOSITE DIRECTION: asked whether CI would ever run on a merge-conflicted head, they polled one branch once a minute for six minutes, observed no run, and reported that GitHub does not create runs for a head it cannot merge -- a NEVER claimed from an instrument whose denominator was one branch and six minutes. ",

    "The control was one command away and refuted it: three other DIRTY pull requests in the same repository carried six and seven check-runs each, while the two heads at zero were simply the two most recently pushed, one dirty and one clean, under a backlog of sixty-two unfinished runs. ",

    "Recency separated the population perfectly and dirtiness did not separate it at all. ",

    "The general form is this row's own, with the sign flipped: there an instrument's GREEN was read as covering a population it never enumerated; here an instrument's SILENCE was. ",

    "A transient state proves nothing about membership without duration or a control already sitting in the state being called impossible -- and DESIGN section 5 names the tell in advance, since NEVER is the word that lets a ratchet pass as a wall. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when an instrument reports a clean round count, ask WHICH ARTIFACTS ITS DENOMINATOR ENUMERATES and whether the artifact you changed is among them -- a per-artifact count is evidence about the artifacts counted and says nothing whatever about the ones the actuator does not own, while reading exactly like whole-population coverage. ",

    "The tell is two actuators over one declared population with no join between their denominators. ",

    "THE FORMER NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER FIRED ON 2026-09-04, AND IS RETIRED BY ITS TRIGGER AND BY NOTHING ELSE. gunbc#10455 deleted RegenPhase from both gunbc.required_ci_phase_roster RequiredCiPhase and its host realization, moved its stage0-mirror adjudicator under the surviving GeneratedArtifactPhase beside the registry-projection adjudicator, runs the second population even when the first refuses, and emits one terminal OK or FAIL naming both populations. A stale projection or drifted mirror now refuses from the SAME phase and neither half can lend its green to the other. ",

    "RUNG: mechanically preventable. The invalid source shape remains writable: the bootstrap host can still omit one component call or reintroduce an independently-green phase, and safety depends on the composite phase executing and its permanent controls staying enrolled. It is therefore not structural guarantee or impossibility. ",

    "EXECUTED EVIDENCE FOR THE CLIMB. The permanent floor-discovered controls refuse both asymmetric states -- registry green with a drifted stage0 mirror, and mirrors green with a stale registry projection -- while an all-clean positive control accepts, excluding a compositor that merely refuses everything. On gunbc#10455's required CI execution the announced phase roster omitted regen and the surviving phase reported `generated-artifact OK populations=registry-projections,stage0-mirrors`; independently, the authoring run observed stage0-mirrors 156/156 clean, continued into a typed registry MemoryStallRefusedPageThrash instead of short-circuiting, and emitted the single terminal composite FAIL naming both populations. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, from mechanically preventable to structurally guaranteed: required-run dispatch and heal-before-push consume an exhaustive adjudicator DERIVED from every arm of gunbc.required_ci_phase_roster DeclaredGeneratedArtifactPopulation, such that adding an arm without an adjudicator is a compile refusal and neither consumer can construct Accepted until every arm returns clean. This is the missing construction; a test that the current two calls remain present would only add another mechanical wall.)",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.whole_generated_artifact_adjudication_test", decl_name: "registry_green_does_not_cover_a_drifted_stage0_mirror", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.whole_generated_artifact_adjudication_test", decl_name: "mirror_green_does_not_cover_a_stale_registry_projection", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.whole_generated_artifact_adjudication_test", decl_name: "both_declared_populations_clean_is_the_only_green", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.bin.claim_executor", decl_name: "run", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
